From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 17:13:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Onefile: exec the child in cached mode, rather than fork and
 wait

With a cached payload, nothing is left to clean up after the child, so the
bootstrap has nothing to wait for. On Linux and macOS it forked, ran the
child and waited, costing every run a second process and its fork and
wait, about 4 ms, and the shell saw WEXITSTATUS of whatever the child left,
read even for a child killed by a signal. The bootstrap now execs the child
in its place: one process, the child's own exit status, and signals that
reach it directly rather than forwarded. NUITKA_ONEFILE_PARENT is unset, so
the child does not start a thread to watch a parent it no longer has.

Temporary-directory mode keeps the fork, to remove the unpacked files once
the child is done; Windows is unchanged.
---
 nuitka/build/static_src/OnefileBootstrap.c | 29 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/nuitka/build/static_src/OnefileBootstrap.c b/nuitka/build/static_src/OnefileBootstrap.c
index 379b311..fa49ebd 100644
--- a/nuitka/build/static_src/OnefileBootstrap.c
+++ b/nuitka/build/static_src/OnefileBootstrap.c
@@ -1837,6 +1837,34 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
     }
 
     cleanupChildProcess(false);
+#else
+#if _NUITKA_ONEFILE_TEMP_BOOL == 0
+    // A cached payload stays where it is: nothing is left to clean up once the
+    // child is done, so there is nothing to wait for either. The child replaces
+    // this process, which saves a fork and a process, and leaves the shell the
+    // child's own exit status, including death by a signal. There is no parent
+    // for the child to watch either.
+    unsetEnvironmentVariable("NUITKA_ONEFILE_PARENT");
+
+    // Make sure, we use the absolute program path for argv[0]
+    argv[0] = (char *)getBinaryPath();
+
+    // On WSL, the AVs can cause this, not sure about Linux in general, but
+    // we can wait for a bit.
+    int retry_count = 0;
+    while (retry_count < 10) {
+        execv(fork_binary, argv);
+
+        if (errno == ETXTBSY) {
+            usleep(100000); // 100ms delay
+            retry_count++;
+        } else {
+            break;
+        }
+    }
+
+    fatalErrorChild("Error, couldn't launch child (exec)", errno);
+    int exit_code = 2;
 #else
     pid_t pid = fork();
     int exit_code;
@@ -1885,6 +1913,7 @@ int main(int argc, char **argv) {
 
         cleanupChildProcess(false);
     }
+#endif
 
 #endif
 
